  "name": "Xuc (Salvadoran dance-band genre)",
  "family": "global",
  "lineage": "Salvadoran dance genre created in the 1940s by the bandleader and composer Francisco 'Paquito' Palaviccini, whose Orquesta Internacional Polío recorded it with a dance-band line-up of trumpets, saxophones, trombones, piano, bass and drums. His 'El carnaval de San Miguel' tied the xuc to the carnival of San Miguel, and it is often described as El Salvador's national dance.",
